<title>COTE D'IVOIRE: African Bank approves $20 mln loan for Kenya dam.</title>
<headline>African Bank approves $20 mln loan for Kenya dam.</headline>
<dateline>ABIDJAN 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The African Development Dam (AfDB) said on Wednesday it had approved a supplementary loan of $20.08 million for Kenya to meet the cost overrun for the construction of the Thika Dam.</p>
<p>The Thika river dam is a major component of the Third Nairobi Water Supply Project, an important phase in the future development of Nairobi water supply to meet the demands of the city's fast growing population, AfDB said.</p>
<p>The project, originally estimated at about $230 million, was initially co-financed by the AfDB, the International Development Association, the European Investment Bank, Japan's cooperation agency OECF and the Nairobi City Council, it added.    --</p>
